WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.957
Your agent forgot 2,396 conversations.

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:06.274
Including what you told it three days ago.

00:00:06.333 --> 00:00:09.150
But now? It can pick up
right where you left off.

00:00:09.233 --> 00:00:10.619
Not one. Not two.

00:00:10.619 --> 00:00:12.213
Not even three.

00:00:12.233 --> 00:00:14.339
But... six agents.

00:00:15.624 --> 00:00:17.149
Thousands of conversations.

00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:18.687
One search. Any agent.

00:00:18.687 --> 00:00:19.928
Any conversation.

00:00:20.945 --> 00:00:25.478
Agent History Search. Put that work back
within reach asking the agent you already use.

00:00:25.533 --> 00:00:32.083
It searches the history on your computer, read-only, with no
account and no servers, and answers with a source you can check.

00:00:32.251 --> 00:00:33.764
Can't remember a tool's name?

00:00:33.764 --> 00:00:35.437
Describe what you used it for.

00:00:36.639 --> 00:00:39.655
Which tool did we use to scan
skills for security last week?

00:00:39.976 --> 00:00:43.712
Your agent searches the saved
conversations and reads matching passages.

00:00:48.023 --> 00:00:49.373
There it is: SkillSpector.

00:00:49.373 --> 00:00:51.173
With the original reference.

00:00:56.477 --> 00:00:58.281
It finds it. Recover a decision.

00:00:58.281 --> 00:01:01.022
Find the fix that worked.
Retrieve the file you delivered.

00:01:02.615 --> 00:01:06.973
Ready to try it? Give your agent the setup
prompt, and choose which histories it may read.

00:01:08.294 --> 00:01:09.819
You already did the work.

00:01:09.819 --> 00:01:11.485
Ask your agent to find it.

00:01:12.058 --> 00:01:13.425
Agent History Search.

00:01:13.425 --> 00:01:14.958
Free and open source.
